d of out in the  exoskeleton  according to the account of Adrian De La  Cruz he planned to bring an end to the  creature by drinking a bottle of Cyanide  and letting it feed upon him it is  unclear if he was successful  in any case the tale of the megalomorpha  continues into the modern era in 2004 a  company charting the sea floor off the  coast of Hawaii discovers an abandoned  remotely operated vehicle the vehicle  was lost during a survey of a sunken  ship with its umbilical cord cut off and  on the vehicle's camera is a photo of a  familiar insect-like creature which  seems to have been the cause of the  vehicle's disappearance and perhaps the  wreck of the ship itself  the final glimpse of the megalomorpha  comes in the form of trail cam pictures  from 2006 recovered from a now defunct  online hunting form as for what happened  to the megalomorpha from here however is  anyone's guess for who can say what  lurks in the dark corners of the world  this brief glimpse into the Striking in  surreal creations of Eduardo Valdez Evia  leaves many questions still unanswered  but according to the artist himself a  mystery is most engaging when there's a  little ambiguity I'm not one for giving  out the whole lore to everybody because  I think that ruins a little bit of the  fun it's that found horror thing where  it makes you like dig for more you're  kind of cursing yourself with knowledge  but you need to know more  if you'd like to discover more of this  mysterious art for yourself there are  links in the description a tremendous  thank you to Eduardo Valdes Evia for  sharing insights into his many projects  once again you can support him on  patreon and follow him on social media  using the links down below  and as always thanks for watching if you  enjoyed this entry please lend your  support by liking subscribing and  hitting the notification icon to stay up  to date on all things curious see you in  the next video  foreign
 

